@baseUrl = https://<your-app-name>.azurewebsites.net
@localUrl = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Home page (unauthenticated) - shows "Log In" button
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### 2. Access /protected WITHOUT a session
# Expect: 302 redirect to /login, and an "unauthorized_attempt" log entry
GET {{baseUrl}}/protected

### 3. Access /profile WITHOUT a session (same guard clause, other protected route)
# Expect: 302 redirect to /login, and an "unauthorized_attempt" log entry
GET {{baseUrl}}/profile

### 4. Start the Auth0 login flow
# Open this one in a BROWSER, not the REST Client, since it redirects to
# Auth0's hosted login page and then back to /callback.
GET {{baseUrl}}/login

### 5. After logging in via the browser, copy the session cookie from dev tools
#    and paste it below to simulate authenticated requests to /protected.
#    Expect: 200 OK, and a "protected_access" log entry with user_id + email
GET {{baseUrl}}/protected
Cookie: <paste-authenticated-session-cookie-here>

### 6. Repeat request #5 more than 10 times within 15 minutes to simulate the
#    "excessive access" scenario the KQL query / alert is designed to catch.
GET {{baseUrl}}/protected
Cookie: <paste-authenticated-session-cookie-here>

### 7. View profile page while authenticated
GET {{baseUrl}}/profile
Cookie: <paste-authenticated-session-cookie-here>

### 8. Logout - should show a "logout" log entry and redirect to Auth0 logout
GET {{baseUrl}}/logout
Cookie: <paste-authenticated-session-cookie-here>

### --- Local testing (run `python app.py`, then hit localhost:5000) ---

### 9. Local: unauthenticated /protected
GET {{localUrl}}/protected

### 10. Local: home page
GET {{localUrl}}/
